	"single-space-marine-chapter": {"category": CATEGORY_ROSTER, "name": "Single Space Marine Chapter", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_space_marines_faction_page_v2_8_1_observed_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "local_checks_pending", "scope": "Current-reference Space Marines army admission rejects units from more than one represented Chapter faction keyword. Non-Faction rule keywords such as DEATHWING/RAVENWING do not by themselves select a Chapter. Shared ADEPTUS ASTARTES profiles without a Chapter remain available. Historical profiles and complete army legality are outside this gate."},
	"marine-detachment-chapter-restrictions": {"category": CATEGORY_ROSTER, "name": "Space Marine detachment Chapter restrictions", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_space_marines_faction_page_v2_8_1_observed_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "local_checks_pending", "scope": "Prepared-match admission restricts Spearpoint Task Force to represented WHITE SCARS faction-keyword profiles; Wrath of the Rock, Darkflight Pursuit and Inner Circle Task Force to DARK ANGELS; Medusa's Wrath to IRON HANDS; and Fist of the God-Emperor to BLACK TEMPLARS. Shared ADEPTUS ASTARTES profiles without a Chapter remain eligible; DEATHWING/RAVENWING conditional rule keywords are outside Chapter classification. These checks do not certify full list legality."},
	"marine-conditional-chapter-keywords": {"category": CATEGORY_ROSTER, "name": "Space Marine conditional Chapter keywords", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_space_marines_faction_page_v2_8_1_observed_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Prepared setup resolves per-player Chapter context and normalizes conditional keywords for current-reference Marine profiles in every match, including when current unit abilities are disabled. It removes source-projected DEATHWING/RAVENWING from shared profile instances, then in Dark Angels context grants DEATHWING to current ADEPTUS ASTARTES TERMINATOR/DREADNOUGHT profiles and listed conditional identities, and RAVENWING to current ADEPTUS ASTARTES MOUNTED or VEHICLE+FLY profiles. Explicit Chapter selections and Chapter-restricted detachments still require current unit abilities. The in-match datasheet shows the effective keywords and identifies conditional Dark Angels grants. Historical/unreconciled profiles are excluded. The resolved Chapter context is stored in the match manifest; saved army setup also retains selections when present, and LAN peers must agree. The conditional rule keywords do not establish Chapter identity. Focused checks, visual review, network validation and full army legality remain pending."},
	"ca-dominance-hammer-fixed": {"category": CATEGORY_MISSION, "name": "CA 2026-27: per-player primary / Hammer / fixed secondaries", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_mission_deck_2026_27_event_companion_v1_3_and_marine_necron_pages_app_2_8_1_checked_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Selected mission with ten primary cards selectable independently for each player: Battlefield Dominance, Immovable Object, Meatgrinder, Destroyer's Wrath, Outmanoeuvre, Delaying Action, Reconnaissance Sweep, Secure Asset, Inescapable Dominion and Sabotage. Each player scores their own card; Secure Asset and Sabotage actions are offered only to the player who selected that card. For the checked Gladius vs Awakened Dynasty profile, each player can choose and save Take and Hold or Priority Assets from the single 3 DP detachment in that roster. Local hot-seat play can seal choices sequentially when both players use matchup defaults; both choices and the primary cards appear after the second lock. Direct overrides use visible setup controls; LAN simultaneous hidden selection is unsupported. Default primaries derive per player from the own-Force-Disposition row and opponent-Force-Disposition column: Take and Hold/Take and Hold gives Battlefield Dominance; Take and Hold/Priority Assets gives Inescapable Dominion; Priority Assets/Take and Hold gives Secure Asset; Priority Assets/Priority Assets gives Sabotage. Either player can select a direct Mission Generator override independently. Other Force Disposition roster combinations are not implemented. Both players share one fixed pair: Engage on All Fronts + Assassination (default), Bring It Down, A Grievous Blow, Secure No Man's Land, No Prisoners, Behind Enemy Lines, Centre Ground, Display of Might, Overwhelming Force, Outflank, Forward Position, Defend Stronghold or A Tempting Target. At each end-of-turn check, Engage on All Fronts, Secure No Man's Land, Behind Enemy Lines and Centre Ground score for the active player; Display of Might awards 2VP to a leading active player or 5VP to a leading non-active player at each turn end; Overwhelming Force, No Prisoners, Bring It Down and A Grievous Blow evaluate qualifying enemy losses for each player; Assassination awards the opponent of each CHARACTER destroyed during the battle. Secure No Man's Land awards 5VP when the active player controls at least two central or expansion objectives at end of turn. No Prisoners awards 2VP per enemy unit destroyed during the turn, up to 5VP at each turn-end scoring check, using the turn-start and turn-end unit-loss snapshot. Behind Enemy Lines awards 3VP per friendly unit wholly in the enemy deployment zone, up to 5VP per turn-end check, excluding AIRCRAFT and Battle-shocked units. Centre Ground awards 5VP if eligible friendly presence is within 3 inches of centre and no enemy unit is within 6 inches, or 3VP if no enemy unit is within 3 inches; friendly AIRCRAFT and Battle-shocked units cannot establish presence, while any enemy unit in range denies it. Range uses nearest base edge and model elevation. Display of Might compares the two player counts of units wholly in No Man's Land at both players' turn ends, awarding 2VP to the leading active player and 5VP to the leading non-active player; AIRCRAFT and Battle-shocked units do not count, and all living model bases must fit in the region. Overwhelming Force awards 3VP per enemy unit destroyed during the turn that was within objective range at turn start, up to 5VP per scoring check, using a turn-start presence snapshot. Outflank awards 3VP for eligible units within 6 inches of a battlefield edge and outside own territory, or 5VP for two units near opposite edges when at least one is outside own territory; edge distance uses the nearest base edge, and a unit is within own territory if any living model base overlaps that player's battlefield half. Forward Position awards 5VP for controlling the opponent's home objective and 5VP for each expansion objective controlled at end of turn. Defend Stronghold awards 3VP to the player whose opponent just ended a turn from battle round two if that player controls their home objective, plus 2VP if no enemy units are within their deployment zone; first-round replacement draws are unsupported. A Tempting Target lets each opponent select one central or expansion objective for the other player after the terrain roll; the target holder scores 5VP at end of turn while controlling it. Delaying Action awards 2VP for each enemy unit destroyed at the end of any turn; from battle round two, it also awards 4VP at the scoring checkpoint for controlling an objective other than either home objective, and 3VP at end of turn for controlling both a central and an expansion objective. Existing scoring caps apply. Immovable Object scores 3VP at end of turn for controlling one or more central objectives, plus 5VP per non-home objective at the Command phase in battle rounds two to four and at end of turn in round five. Destroyer's Wrath scores 3VP if any enemy unit was destroyed that turn; from battle round two, it also awards 4VP for controlling one or more non-home objectives at the checkpoint, 6VP for controlling more objectives than the opponent, and 4VP when current enemy unit losses exceed the player's friendly losses from the previous turn. Outmanoeuvre awards 10VP at end of turn for controlling the opponent's home objective, 4VP per non-home objective at the end of battle round one, 5VP per non-home objective at the end of the Command phase in rounds two and three, and 6VP per non-home objective at end of turn from round four onward. Bring It Down scores 4VP per enemy W10+ model alive at turn start and destroyed by turn end. A Grievous Blow scores 4VP per enemy unit with battle-start Starting Strength 13+ that was alive at turn start and destroyed by turn end, up to 5VP. Sabotage awards 3VP for each unit that completed its action this turn, plus 2VP for each such unit within range of an objective in opponent territory; from round two it also awards 4VP at the checkpoint if you control a non-home objective. Its Shooting-phase action is unlimited, requires different objectives for each unit starting it that phase, and completes at end of turn only if the unit controls that objective. Existing scoring caps apply; both opposing rosters must include a qualifying target when Bring It Down or A Grievous Blow is selected. First-round and no-target replacement draws and mid-turn restored or newly created targets are unsupported. No points legality certification."},
