	"heroic-intervention": {"category": CATEGORY_STRATAGEM, "name": "Heroic Intervention (15.11)", "supported": true, "validation_status": "tests_passed_local_targeted", "scope": "Core; end of opponent Charge. Leap to Defend 1 CP or Into the Fray +1 CP with charge cap 6", "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_22"},
	"counteroffensive": {"category": CATEGORY_STRATAGEM, "name": "Counteroffensive (15.12)", "supported": true, "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Core; 2 CP in the opponent's Fight phase, immediately after an enemy unit has resolved its attacks. One eligible friendly unit gains Fights First and must be the next unit selected to fight. The post-fight response is limited to the normal attacks step; a forced consolidation-reaction fight takes place during the active player's own Fight phase and cannot open Counteroffensive. Transhuman Swiftness handles its separately supported Tacticus queue continuation. Focused checks remain pending.", "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_26"},
	# Core attack rules, missions and geometry.
	"shooting-at-engaged-monsters-vehicles": {"category": CATEGORY_ATTACK_RULE, "name": "Shooting at engaged Monsters and Vehicles (17.03)", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_june_2026_checked_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "In the controlling player's own Shooting phase, an unengaged unit can target an engaged enemy MONSTER/VEHICLE with ranged attacks except BLAST; apply -1 to Hit except for CLOSE-QUARTERS attacks from a unit engaged with that target. Units already engaged must use their eligible Close-quarters shooting and can target only enemy units their unit is engaged with. The engaged-target exception is not granted by this rule during out-of-phase shooting. Focused local checks and playtesting remain pending."},
	"custom-training-mission": {"category": CATEGORY_MISSION, "name": "Custom training mission", "supported": true, "source_status": "project_authored_training_profile", "validation_status": "tests_passed_local_targeted", "scope": "Project-owned custom training scenario and objective scoring; separate from current Chapter Approved mission certification."},
	"desperate-escape-heavy-hazard": {"category": CATEGORY_MOVEMENT, "name": "Desperate Escape all-heavy Hazard rolls", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Core Rules §§06.03 and 09.07. Desperate Escape makes one Hazard roll per model. Each failed 1–2 causes three mortal wounds when every living model in the unit is MONSTER or VEHICLE; otherwise it causes one. The multiplier is applied to the initial roll pool and recalculated after an optional Command Re-roll, then wounds use the existing Mortal Wounds allocation and prevention path. Other Hazard modifiers and ability/stratagem exceptions remain outside this capability. Focused local checks and playtesting are pending."},
	"transport-disembark-hazard-rolls": {"category": CATEGORY_TRANSPORT, "name": "Combat and Emergency Disembark Hazard rolls", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Core Rules §§06.02–06.03, 15.02 and 18.04–18.05. Combat Disembark and Emergency Disembark make one Hazard roll per passenger model; each failed 1–2 inflicts three mortal wounds instead of one when every living passenger model is MONSTER or VEHICLE. When the configured core stratagem is eligible, the passenger's owner may accept the pool or use Command Re-roll on one die before allocating wounds. The passenger's owner allocates the resulting wounds through the shared mortal-wound prevention path before placement. Rapid, Tactical, Assault and Shock Disembark do not make these Hazard rolls. Focused local checks and playtesting are pending; broader transport abilities and Deadly Demise remain outside this capability."},
	"upper-floor-movement-training": {"category": CATEGORY_GEOMETRY, "name": "Bounded terrain-floor movement and visibility (training slice)", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Supported surfaces are the default terrain-11e-v1 central ruin floor, 3-inch first-floor proxies in the Dense ruins of Event Companion layouts A/B/C, and the 3-inch and 6-inch project-authored surfaces in the optional multi-storey objective-training layout. Event Companion diagrams do not define their floor dimensions or heights; they are project-authored training proxies following the Core Rules' general 3-inch first-floor convention. The optional 6-inch surface is exercise geometry. Movement, Charge, Pile-in and Consolidation placement support eligible INFANTRY, BEASTS, SWARM and FLY models. Ordinary vertical moves stay within 1/2 inch horizontally of a listed ruin wall and count vertical distance; Take to the Skies lets FLY models ignore wall access and vertical distance only during an eligible declared move. Equipped Reiver units with Grapnel Launchers ignore vertical distance and move through models while retaining wall access. Every base must fit wholly on the destination surface. Coherency, Engagement Range, objective-marker height and placement feedback account for elevation. Bounded 3D cylindrical-proxy visibility and Plunging Fire are supported between ground and these floors: eligible attackers at least 3 inches above ground gain BS +1 against a visible unit containing a ground-level model; TOWERING can qualify within 12 inches and AIRCRAFT are excluded. Core Snap Shooting requires an unmodified 6 regardless of BS, except where another rule sets a different threshold. MONSTER terrain paths, surfaces above the fixed training heights, arbitrary vertical paths and exact imported-mesh visibility remain unsupported. Local checks and playtesting are pending."},
	"monster-vehicle-model-passage": {"category": CATEGORY_MOVEMENT, "name": "MONSTER/VEHICLE passage through models", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Core Rules §17.01: during Normal Moves and Advances, each MONSTER or VEHICLE model may pass through friendly and enemy models except other MONSTER/VEHICLE models. The shared Movement-phase validator and the supported Purgation Run Normal Move apply passage and blocking per moving model and move type; endpoint overlap and the ordinary terrain, distance, coherency and end-of-move gates remain. This does not extend the permission to Charge, Pile-in, Consolidation or other move types. Focused local checks and playtesting are pending."},
	"take-to-the-skies-movement": {"category": CATEGORY_GEOMETRY, "name": "Take to the Skies", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_26", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Core Rules §§21.03 and 24.17. When a FLYING unit is selected for a Normal Move, Advance, Fall Back or Charge, the active player may declare Take to the Skies before movement; for Advance and Charge, before rolling. Declared FLY models can move through all models and terrain while ignoring vertical distance. Reduce the unit's maximum distance by 2 inches, except when it has HOVER. The declaration persists through movement/charge stratagem and roll decisions, is included in Charge target range, and is checked by shared placement validation. Ordinary FLY moves retain normal terrain and vertical-distance rules. Bounded 3D visibility and Plunging Fire cover the default central ruin and Event Companion A/B/C Dense ruin proxies and the fixed 3-inch and 6-inch floors in the optional local objective practice layout; arbitrary surfaces and exact-mesh visibility remain unsupported. Focused local checks and playtesting are pending."},
	"multi-storey-training-terrain": {"category": CATEGORY_GEOMETRY, "name": "Multi-storey local objective training terrain", "supported": true, "source_status": "wahapedia_e11_core_rules_current_2026_10_26_plus_project_authored_layout", "validation_status": "implemented_local_checks_pending", "scope": "Optional local objective-training layout with central ruin surfaces at 3 and 6 inches. Uses the existing supported vertical-access, vertical-distance, whole-base fit, elevated-visibility and Plunging Fire paths. The platform dimensions and wall geometry are project-authored practice proxies, not Event Companion measurements. Only currently supported model keywords can use the upper surfaces; arbitrary imported terrain, other floor heights and broader vertical movement remain unsupported. Focused local checks and human review are pending."},
	"upper-floors": {"category": CATEGORY_GEOMETRY, "name": "Complete upper floors and vertical battlefield geometry", "supported": false, "validation_status": "not_supported", "scope": "Bounded support now includes the project-authored 3-inch and 6-inch surfaces in the multi-storey objective-training layout and the 3-inch floors in Event Companion layouts A/B/C. Exact Event Companion terrain measurements, arbitrary other upper surfaces, unrestricted vertical movement, exact imported-mesh visibility and a battlefield editor remain unsupported."},
